the future.","published":"2023-02-26T12:16:21.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/detroit-lions/post/_/id/38953/no-hockenson-no-problem-lions-success-at-te-offers-optimism-for-2023-beyond","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No Hockenson, no problem: Lions' success at TE offers optimism for 2023, beyond","description":"The Lions managed nicely after the unpopular T.J. Hockenson trade, unearthing a trio if productive -- and affordable -- tight ends for the future.","published":"2023-02-26T11:20:10.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/detroit-lions/post/_/id/38953/no-hockenson-no-problem-lions-success-at-te-offers-optimism-for-2023-beyond","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No Hockenson, no problem: Lions' success at TE offers optimism for 2023, beyond","description":"The Lions managed nicely after the unpopular T.J. Hockenson trade, unearthing a trio if productive -- and affordable -- tight ends for the future.","published":"2023-02-26T11:00:03.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/detroit-lions/post/_/id/38953/no-hockenson-no-problem-lions-success-at-te-offers-optimism-for-2023-beyond","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No Hockenson, no problem: Lions' success at TE offers optimism for 2023, beyond","description":"The Lions managed nicely after the unpopular T.J. Hockenson trade, unearthing a trio if productive -- and affordable -- tight ends for the future.","published":"2023-02-25T02:39:51.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/detroit-lions/post/_/id/38953/no-hockenson-no-problem-lions-success-at-te-offers-optimism-for-2023-beyond","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"'We fully believe in each other': Detroit Lions continue playoff push with late win vs. Jets","description":"The word “believe” rolled off the tongues of many players inside the Lions’ locker room as they find themselves in the thick of the playoff hunt.","published":"2022-12-20T14:54:40.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/detroit-lions/post/_/id/38906/detroit-lions-fully-believe-in-each-other-after-late-win-vs-jets","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Brock Wright","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brock_Wright","description":"American football player (born 1998)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:16Z","intro":"Brock Joseph Wright (born November 27, 1998) is an American professional football tight end and fullback for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Wright played college football at the University of Notre Dame, where he appeared in 48 games with 11 starts. He had seven receptions for 78 yards and one touchdown during his career with the Fighting Irish."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"On May 1, 2021, Wright signed with the Detroit Lions as an undrafted free agent after the 2021 NFL draft. On October 23, Wright was activated from the practice squad by the Lions for the team's week 7 game against the Los Angeles Rams. He was signed to the active roster on November 8. On December 5, Wright scored his first NFL touchdown against the Minnesota Vikings on a 23-yard pass from Jared Goff.\nOn December 18, 2022, in a Week 15 game at the New York Jets, Wright scored the go-ahead touchdown on a 51-yard pass from Goff on 4th down and inches with 1:49 remaining in the game. The Lions held on for the 20–17 win — improving their record to 7–7 and keeping their playoff hopes alive in the NFC.\nAs a restricted free agent in 2024, the San Francisco 49ers signed Wright to a three-year, $12 million offer sheet. Five days later, the Lions matched the offer, and Wright re-signed with Detroit on April 3, 2024.\nIn 2025, Wright made 11 appearances (eight starts) for the Lions, recording 14 receptions for 108 yards and two touchdowns. On December 4, 2025, Wright was placed on injured reserve due to a neck injury."}],"wikidataId":"Q109220124","social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4242392","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/W/WrigBr01.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/brock-wright/60994","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/brock-wright/9878","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brock_Wright"},"insights":["On the field for 48% of Detroit’s offensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $4.7M is the 15th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Entered the league in 2021 as an undrafted free agent."]}